		     section 1.7, section 6.2). The Dock highlights the icon only for types the app claims,
		     and the compress gesture has to accept any file or folder, so this last group claims
		     public.item and public.folder. `CFBundleTypeRole = Viewer` + `LSHandlerRank = None` is
		     the documented "can open it, must never be its default handler" pair; `Shell` would
		     also grant the drop but means "provides runtime services for other processes", which is
		     not what this is. It claims no extension, so it never competes with the 39 association
		     groups above. `DockDropRouter.action` then routes a single recognised archive to an
		     open and everything else to the compress command. -->
